<title>USA: Albright stresses need for NATO enlargement.</title>
<headline>Albright stresses need for NATO enlargement.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Secretary of State Madeleine Albright on Friday stressed the U.S. desire for NATO enlargement, but also emphasised the need to resolve differences with Russia over the issue.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that it is essential to enlarge NATO,&quot; Albright said at her first news conference as secretary. &quot;We understand that the Russians have some problems with it. But what is clear is that both countries are committed to working this situation out and develping mutual understanding based on our national interests.&quot;</p>
</text>
